Secure MCP Server - Confluence Data Integration

Project Overview
Build a secure Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that:

Core Function
Retrieves Confluence content and exposes it as MCP Resources to MCP-compatible LLM clients.

Security Requirements
	• Expose Resources only (NOT Tools)
	• OAuth 2.1 authentication using Okta
	• Azure Key Vault for secret management
	• Least Privilege enforcement
	• End-user identity propagation
	• Trust Boundary Enforcement
	• Audit Logging
	• Rate Limiting
	• Schema Validation
	• Output Sanitization
	
Development Constraints
During development:
	• No direct connectivity to Okta
	• No direct connectivity to Azure Key Vault
	• No direct connectivity to Confluence
Therefore:
	• Mock Okta
	• Mock Azure Key Vault
	• Mock Confluence
will be used during development.
Production deployment will replace mocks with real implementations.

